  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> at rest splits into two parts having masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The ratio of de Broglie wavelength of two parts will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MkHTx",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
